Spec: Android owned direct and relay routes

Purpose:
  Compose exact authorized service scopes with private packaged FRP visitors.

Owns:
  ./FrpRoutes.java

References:
  ./FrpRuntimeBridge.sdd
  ./ServerSettings.sdd

Must:
  Match the fifteen-second transport heartbeat response timeout used by Windows; retain explicit authorization expiry and network-generation invalidation.
  Invalidate all owned cached sessions on a changed default-network generation, preserving the pool's capacity and late-creation cleanup rules.
  Share one runtime only across completely equal local authority snapshots; release each stream independently, retain used idle sessions at most sixty seconds and revoke pooled resources when their exact authority changes.
  Generate each private visitor from approved Agent scope and deterministic public service names; application SDKs cannot supply backend configuration or ports.
  Use an independent canonical runtime instance ID within the authenticated application namespace and cap creating, running and closing owned runtimes at sixteen.
  Bind loopback only, disable proxy environment use and keep inner peer mTLS and current server leases necessary for business bytes.
  Bound each waiter by its original open deadline, close late shared starts after their last waiter leaves, and remove only generated private profiles.

  Keep failed cleanup counted against capacity; bound post-stop cleanup retries to three seconds and never readmit retired resources.

  Build direct and relay visitors inside the same exact-scope child, enable XTCP only with explicit STUN destinations and never configure implicit visitor fallback.
  A direct-only import has no STCP visitor; route leases expose only their selected private loopback port.
